/**
 * \author Mr.Nobody
 * \file ItTest_ModBus.cpp
 * \ingroup ModBus
 * \brief Integration tests of ModBus RTU stack on target (master <-> slave).
 *
 * ModBus master (master transport layer) and ModBus slave (complete slave
 * stack - transport layer, application core, function handlers, diagnostics)
 * run on the same MCU, each one on its own USART. The USARTs are cross
 * connected by wires on the board, so every frame passes real USART hardware
 * (USART MCAL, interrupt / DMA data handling, receiver timeout as end of frame
 * detection).
 *
 * Requests are generated by the test (address + PDU), CRC is calculated by the
 * test independently of the stack. Every exchange is checked on both sides:
 * - Request received by the slave (raw bytes incl. CRC) is equal to the request
 *   generated by the test and to the frame transmitted by the master.
 * - Response received by the master (raw bytes incl. CRC) is equal to the
 *   response expected by the test (model of slave data) and to the response
 *   passed to the application by the master transport layer.
 * - Slave application data (registers, coils) are equal to the model.
 *
 * Required wiring (NUCLEO-H503RB):
 *
 *      Master USART1 TX  PB14  ------>  PB1  USART2 RX  Slave
 *      Master USART1 RX  PB15  <------  PA2  USART2 TX  Slave
 *
 * Used resources (see board configuration below):
 * - USART1 (master), USART2 (slave), USART interrupts
 * - GPDMA1 channels 0 - 3 (DMA mode test cases)
 * - TIM2 - 1 ms time base of ModBus tasks
 * - TIM6 - detection of debug halts (runs while the core is halted)
 *
 * Debug halts: the host (probe-rs) halts the core for a few milliseconds on
 * every read of the result mailbox. Interrupts are not served during the halt,
 * the USART receiver can overrun and frames get lost. TIM2 is frozen during
 * the halt, TIM6 is not - their difference is the halt time. Exchange with
 * transport failure (USART error, lost frame, unexpected request status)
 * during which the core was halted is repeated (max. 3 times, reported by
 * INFO line) - in place in random sequences (all generated requests are
 * idempotent), otherwise the whole test case after reset (next stage).
 * Failure without halt and wrong content of a complete frame always fail the
 * test case (INFO line with the measured halt time).
 */

